\subsection{Gap Analysis}

Existing literature provides strong foundations in educational data mining, mentoring effectiveness, and recommendation algorithms. However, most studies address these domains independently rather than integrating them into a unified academic mentorship ecosystem. Many peer mentoring studies lack automated behavioural data tracking, while recommendation research often overlooks structured mentorship lifecycle modeling. Additionally, practical systems frequently struggle with cold-start limitations, transparency issues, and ethical concerns in algorithmic decision-making.

MentorLink addresses these gaps by combining structured mentorship workflows, interaction-level transactional logging, and an analytics-ready backend within a single institute-exclusive platform. By integrating behavioural data capture with scalable recommendation and mining mechanisms, the proposed system bridges the divide between theoretical EDM research and practical mentorship platform implementation.

