\subsection{Algorithmic Techniques Used}



\subsubsection{1. Mentorship Lifecycle State Machine}

The mentorship process follows a finite state machine model:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Requested
    \item Accepted
    \item Active
    \item Closed
\end{itemize}

State transitions are strictly controlled to ensure system consistency.

\subsubsection{2. Structured Interaction Logging Model}

Each mentorship session is logged with metadata:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Topic
    \item Category
    \item Timestamp
    \item Duration
    \item Participants
\end{itemize}

This structured logging enables future application of data mining techniques such as:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Clustering
    \item Association Rule Mining
    \item Trend Analysis
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Design Principles Followed}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Separation of Concerns
    \item Modular Architecture
    \item Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
    \item Scalability-Oriented Backend Design
    \item Analytics-Ready Data Structuring
\end{itemize}

